 "notes": "Direct access, no proxy needed: Shopify storefront, plain requests with a desktop Chrome UA returned HTTP 200 on every URL. Site 429s above roughly 1 request/4s so all fetches were paced at 4.5s. Tree source: the homepage mega-menu HTML (details.header__menu-disclosure > ul.mega-menu__linklist), parsed in full for all 12 top-level departments; furniture lives in the 'Furniture' department (Living Room / Dining Room / Bedroom / Office / Custom Upholstery), the 'Outdoor' department (Outdoor Lounge / Outdoor Dining) and one node under 'Kids'. QTY METHOD: every qty is the storefront's own rendered listing header <p class=\"collection-toolbar__products-count\">N products</p>. Shopify products_count was NOT used anywhere. Independent verification: sofas, dining-tables, outdoor-ottomans and kids-nursery-furniture were re-counted by paging /collections/<handle>/products.json?limit=250 to exhaustion and matched the header exactly 4/4 (53/39/6/33). SANITY: counts vary per collection (3..77) so no site-wide constant; every page's h1 matched the collection requested (e.g. h1 'Beds and Headboards' for beds-headboards), so no silent parent-serving; no round numbers/display caps. Parent-vs-children: all-living-room=382 vs children 466, all-dining-room=187 vs 207, all-bedroom=151 vs 162, all-custom-upholstery=159 vs 142, all-furniture=882 - children sums exceed parents because products belong to several collections, as expected on this store; no parent number was ever copied to a child. EXCLUDED as grouping/nav parents (recorded as is_group rows, no qty): Living Room, Dining Room, Bedroom, Office, Custom Upholstery, Kids & Nursery, Outdoor Lounge, Outdoor Dining. EXCLUDED per s3 'never extract': all 'All ...' landing pages (all-furniture 882, all-living-room 382, all-dining-room 187, all-bedroom 151, all-custom-upholstery 159, all-outdoor 229, all-kids-nursery), Best Sellers, New Furniture, In Stock & Ready to Ship Furniture, every clearance-* collection, all /pages/shop